{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Because they did not meet you with bread and water.</b> It is the way of the world to greet those who come on the road with food and drink — not that Israel lacked anything in the wilderness, for the manna descended for them and the well went with them." "<b>And the Ramban, of blessed memory, wrote:</b> Scripture distanced these two brothers who were recipients of the kindness of Abraham, who saved their father and mother from sword and captivity, and in whose merit the Holy One, blessed be He, brought them out from the overturning (of Sodom). They were obligated to do good to Israel, yet they did evil to them: the one (Moab) hired Balaam son of Beor against them, and the other (Ammon) did not meet them with bread and water. Now Ammon was more wicked in this matter, for when the Moabites and the children of Esau learned that Israel had been warned not to wage war against them, they brought out bread and water for them, but Ammon refused to do so. This is the meaning of ״אשר לא קדמו״ — that they did not go out to meet them with bread and water as the others did. Therefore Scripture put Ammon first and mentioned its offense first — ״על דבר אשר לא קדמו״ — and afterward mentioned Moab and its sin: ״ואשר שכר עליך״. End quote. And our Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded: ״עמוני ולא עמונית, מואבי ולא מואבית״ — 'an Ammonite (male) and not an Ammonitess; a Moabite (male) and not a Moabitess' — because it is a man's way to go out to meet (travelers), but it is not a woman's way to do so, meaning to bring out food outside the border of the land. And this is the basis for permitting Ruth the Moabitess, from whom David descended."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:50:34.922447888Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}